# Cards are data

All Descent content is **YAML in `content/`**, passed through `content-lint`
and compiled to a bundle. All combat content is the manifest
(`.llm/rules/manifest.mdc`). Nothing else is content.

**No rules in the shell.** The shell draws what the API returns and sends taps
back. It does not decide what an action does, what a gate means, what a die
scores, or when a fight ends. If the shell needs to know something to draw
correctly, the API must return it — that is a finding against the API, not a
licence to reimplement the rule in the renderer.

**No content in the engines.** `src/core` holds no scene ids, no object names,
no prose, no die names, no balance numbers. It knows the two languages and
nothing about the labyrinth.

The seam is the architecture. It is what lets a content author write rooms
without reading TypeScript, an engine card change behaviour without touching
prose, a balance pass run as a data diff, and the draw engine arrange authored
rooms it cannot rewrite.
